    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0316" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.91/102: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-15T18:00:00+03:25">January 15, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 16—3:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18 [<hi rendition="#italic">28?</hi>]. Today I interviewed Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="8" xml:id="d312-f1"/> regarding Department’s telegram No.
                    23 dated January 13, 11 p.m. and he assured me his Government is “flattered by,
                    appreciative of and thoroughly agreeable to” proposal to raise our respective
                    Legations to Embassies. He stated he was immediately telegraphing this favorable
                    attitude to his Minister at Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d312-f1" n="8" xml:id="d312-f1-content">
                <p>Mohammed Saed.</p>
